## Issues fixed on the spot

- A1: aligned `openOODA/audit/foundation_rollup.oot` placeholders with actual line counts.
- A2: corrected 3 demo script paths in `demo_rollup.oot` so they match the filenames shipped in Wave 2.
- A3: removed 4 stale `.sh` artifacts from the Wave 3-4 allowlist that no longer exist.
- A4: rewrote 2 Wave 5 scripts that had academy-style violations (missing `Logline:` line).
- A5: fixed 6 broken cross-references in `SCRIPTING.oot` and `COOKBOOK.oot` (links to non-existent `*.oo` files).
- A6: bumped `script_lint.oo` version trailer from `v0.3` to `v0.4` to match the released template.
- A8: pre-existing parse errors at import resolution are isolated to the broken build path; not regressions.
- A11: trimmed 1 file over 256 lines; no `.md` files; no secrets; no sludge.

## Issues escalated to SPRINT (via [SPRINT-NOTE])

- [SPRINT-NOTE] `sh.oo` is unsafe by design — 19/20 functions are shell-injection sinks. Migration to native `fs_*` ops under typed caps is tracked as a post-migration B-task (DE10).
- [SPRINT-NOTE] Build path is broken. The `.oo` files are source-of-truth text; the `.sh` files are the runnable artifact. Seed rebuild must be fixed before any `.sh` deletion can land.
- [SPRINT-NOTE] F20 phantom detection is correct: 5 files in the allowlist now miss `std/sh.oo` and `std/scenario.oo`. Allowlist needs a refresh.
- [SPRINT-NOTE] Some agents flagged academy-style "literal transliteration" patterns (e.g. preserved bash idioms verbatim). A pass to rewrite 12 scripts in idiomatic `.oo` is queued.
- [SPRINT-NOTE] No `.sh` files were deleted in Wave 7 per the broken build path. Deletion is blocked on the seed rebuild fix.

## Carry-over

- sh.oo is unsafe by design (DE10). 19/20 functions are shell-injection sinks.
- Build path is broken. .oo files are source-of-truth text; .sh files are runnable.
- F20 phantom detection is correct (5 files in allowlist now miss std/sh.oo and std/scenario.oo).
- Some agents flagged academy-style "literal transliteration" patterns.

